A||N||5||WhiteFieroBlur||Does my car sound bad?||||1||
Z||000000||WhiteFieroBlur||12-02-2001||06:58 PM||||Well I am having some car trouble and this is how my car drives.<P> Put in the key but just to on and the battery reads in the red, but starts up normal and fine. Sometimes it struggles to start. Car idles around 1500 and goes down below 1,000 when warm. When at idle the car idles fast around 700-900 rpms back and forth. Battery reads fine. Never goes before 13. Oil pressure reads 38 and will go crazy sometimes but oil pressure never comes on. I let my car sit idle untill the fan kicks it. fan kicks in at around 223 and my car almost seems like its gonna stall and cut off. I can also hear a humming noise when I am in the car. When I drive and slow down in second gear it bucks back and forth pretty bad. As I press on the brakes I can see my lights dim and the humming noise changes as I press and depress the brake. Idle is still moving back and forth sometimes fast sometimes slow but always in the 700-900 range. I can also hear loud engines noises coming from my speakers with the radio on. <P> So thats how my car acts, is this some thing I should worry about or if I take it to the shop it should be fixed easy. <P> thanx||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||12-02-2001||08:19 PM||||Sounds like the alternator is going bad.  Also the oil pressure sender.. if the gauge twitches all over the place it's going bad too.  But a bad alternator can cause all sorts of wierd problems, including hunting idle. <P>When the fan kicks in it puts a big load on the alt, even with a new alternator and fairly new battery in my GT the lights would dim and idle drop for a moment while the engine compensated for the load.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||REDHOTT88||12-02-2001||08:44 PM||||Standard.. you are probably right on with the alternator, but I would also check out the "voltage regulator".||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||12-02-2001||09:24 PM||||The Fiero alternator has a built in voltage regulator. <BR>If you hear a whistle in your speakers that varies with engine speed, you most likely have a bad rectifier in the alternator electronics. (There are three, I believe.)<BR>Will also make your voltage levels do funny things, as electrical stuff is switched on and off.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||WhiteFieroBlur||12-02-2001||10:52 PM||||So why would my alternator be going bad? its like only a lil over a year old. Can it be my system that pushing it over the limits? I don't wanna keep buying one every year. Also My alternator hums really loud. Am I suppose to be hearing it? ||||reg||1
Z||000005||johnt671||12-03-2001||10:51 AM||||Make sure you get the right alt. for your car.  I have air in mine but the last time I got an alt. the parts store gave me one for a car w/o air even though I told them it had air.  Two years later I got to replace it again.  ||||reg||1
